{% set homeowner_guide %}
<p>Quick reference for New Market homeowners:</p>

<p><strong>Small community, same standards:</strong> Don't settle for whoever will show up. You deserve the same quality work as any subdivision in Madison. If a contractor seems surprised you're calling from New Market, that tells you something.</p>

<p><strong>Older home reality check:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Fascia condition matters — rot hides behind gutters</li>
<li>Original gutters from the 70s/80s are past due for replacement</li>
<li>Sectional gutters leak; seamless don't</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Tree debris management:</strong> Heavy tree coverage means one of two things: gutter guards or regular cleaning. Without protection, expect to clean 3-4 times per year minimum — more if you have pines.</p>

<p><strong>Seasonal priorities:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>March:</strong> Pre-storm season check — winter can hide problems</li>
<li><strong>November:</strong> Post-leaf drop cleaning before first freeze</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Warning signs to watch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Overflow during moderate rain = blockage or undersized gutters</li>
<li>Visible sag = failing hangers or fascia damage</li>
<li>Staining on siding = chronic overflow</li>
<li>Erosion near foundation = downspouts not doing their job</li>
</ul>

